=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
Exhaustive testing found no network fault matching the reported symptom. Laptop0 (172.16.20.10/24, switch1 port eth7) is correctly placed in the br_vlan20 bridge domain on switch1, with its uplink carried as tagged VLAN 20 through the switch1→mswitch1 trunk (eth0.20). The 172.16.10.x group (pc4, pc5, laptop2, laptop3) sits in the br_vlan10 bridge domain on the same physical switch1. Inter-VLAN routing is performed by router0, which terminates both VLAN sub-interfaces: eth0.10 (172.16.10.1/24) for VLAN 10 and eth0.20 (172.16.20.1/24) for VLAN 20. The routing table on router0 has directly connected routes for both subnets and no firewall rules in any iptables chain (INPUT, FORWARD, OUTPUT — all policy ACCEPT, zero entries). Ebtables on switch1 and mswitch1 are also completely empty. Laptop0 successfully ARPs its gateway (172.16.20.1, confirmed via arping), pings are bidirectional with zero packet loss to every reachable 172.16.10.x host (pc4 at .4, pc5 at .5, laptop2 at .12, laptop3 at .13), and a traceroute confirms the correct two-hop path: laptop0 → 172.16.20.1 (router0) → destination. No ACL, no VLAN mis-assignment, no firewall rule, and no routing gap was found. The network is operating as designed; the reported connectivity loss is not present at this time.
=== END ===